    "physical_description": "Cone-shaped hood (Thai. khlum pak)of broad central royal blue silk satin band with borders of white, pale green, rose and pale green satin above and below it.  A tassel of royal blue satin and gilt cord forms the finial. Patterned with applique embroidery in gilt parchment framed with gold wire.  The whole lined with red silk. These hoods are used in the Thai royal court to cover a pedestal tray or a bowl, often containing food or offerings. ",
